Fill the entire background with one flat, uniform, fully opaque pure magenta, RGB 255 0 255, hex #FF00FF, edge to edge. The background must be that exact single colour and nothing else: no grey-and-white checkerboard pattern, no white, no grey, no gradient, no texture, no vignette, no ground plane, no cast shadow, no glow or halo bleeding into it. Magenta appears nowhere on the subject itself. Use a landscape canvas exactly twice as wide as it is tall (2:1 aspect ratio, for example 2048x1024).

Game status-effect icon sprite for a 2.5D faceted low-poly papercraft game, matching the exact rendering technique of the attached reference images.

Rendering technique, required exactly as in the references:
- Build every shape from flat polygonal facet planes, like cut and folded paper. One flat, completely solid color per plane. Hard, sharp creases between adjacent planes.
- No smooth 3D shading, no soft gradient across a plane, no gloss, no specular highlight, no surface texture, no surface grain, no photographic noise, no painterly brushwork, no airbrush, no glow, no bloom.
- If the result could be mistaken for a rendered 3D model, a photo, or a digital painting, it is wrong. It must look built from cut and folded matte paper facets.
- One soft light source from the upper left of EACH shape: a broad flat highlight facet on the upper-left side of every fragment, a broad flat shadow facet on the lower-right side. Nothing else.
- No outer contour line and no ink outline anywhere. Shapes separate from each other only by flat color value.
- Restrained saturation, mid-to-high value. Nothing muddy, nothing neon.

Two-frame layout, required exactly:
- The canvas is split by an invisible vertical line exactly at its horizontal midpoint into two equal square panels: a LEFT panel (frame 1) and a RIGHT panel (frame 2). Do not draw the dividing line, a border, a seam, or any frame around either panel — it stays implied only by empty magenta.
- Frame 1 and Frame 2 show the exact same subject, drawn at the exact same overall scale and the exact same overall bounding size, centered the same way inside its own panel. Keep every fragment at least 10% of the panel width away from the vertical midline and from the panel's outer edges, so nothing crosses the seam and nothing touches the border.
- The ONLY differences allowed between Frame 1 and Frame 2: each fragment is rotated in place by a small angle (5 to 15 degrees, some clockwise, some counter-clockwise, never uniform), each fragment shifts position by only a tiny amount (at most 4% of the panel width, to suggest a gentle drip settling), and the highlight/shadow split on a fragment may shift slightly. The overall silhouette size, the overall bounding box, and the hollow empty center MUST stay identical between the two panels. Never make Frame 2's cluster larger, smaller, or shifted off-center compared to Frame 1.

Subject identity, shared by both frames: a WET / SOAKED status-effect marker that will be composited above a creature sprite in-game — never as a background element, always as a small floating overlay icon. Five separate flat water fragments: two or three flattened puddle-splash blobs (a low rounded splash shape, wider than tall, as if a droplet just landed and spread, built from 3 to 4 flat facet planes each) of clearly different sizes, plus two or three small separate round droplet fragments (simple rounded teardrop facet shapes, much smaller than the splash blobs). Scatter all fragments loosely around a completely empty center in an irregular, asymmetric arrangement — never a perfect radial star, never mirror-symmetric, never touching or overlapping each other. The empty center must stay clear so a creature drawn underneath this icon remains readable. Palette: highlight #E8F7EE, pale cyan #98DEEB, mid blue #6FCCF4, blue #53B2EB, deep blue shadow #2D92E4 — use only these five colors, one flat color per facet.

Exclusions: no lightning, no fire, no leaf, no stone, no circle ring, no closed loop, no wave shape, no cloud, no rain streak lines, no card border, no icon plate, no dish, no coin shape, no text, no frame, no watermark, no logo, no creature, no face. Silhouette of each fragment must stay clearly readable when shrunk to 64 pixels wide.
